# lobo, the web server in wolf (wolffe-lang/lobo, public), at the commit
# tests/mpx4-unix runs its control client from (px34): trunk 944edc1,
# 0.1.3 with the channel flipped to +dev. tools/mklobo builds it as lobo
# builds itself, with the toolchain THAT tree pins (wolf-toolchain.toml:
# wolf 0.2.27, pin 0ddda6b; wolf-std 14f0ab2), the wolf archive taken by
# the digest below (lobo's file names the version line, the digest is
# the release asset's own, the same kernel/wolf.pin names).
LOBO_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/lobo
# px65 (2026-10-23): lobo trunk 49ed870 (v0.1.5 and 38 commits after it,
# +dev; ws-r40p): its own toolchain to wolf 0.2.35 (pin cf0c13d) / lupin
# 0.1.56 / wolf-std 2386522e; since v0.1.5 a master refuses replacement
# workers once its binary's identity changed (101a2a8), and the pins.
# px97 (2026-11-04): lobo trunk 64e7339 (25 commits after 49ed870, +dev): its
# own toolchain to wolf 0.2.36 (pin 5adf3d9) / lupin 0.1.58 / wolf-std
# 78b9d3cb, and an incomplete reload of dropped workers reported as a
# failure (lobo#101). No lobo release after v0.1.5 yet, so the
# release build below is unchanged.
# px97 (2026-11-06): lobo trunk 39788b86, 57 commits after 64e7339d (6 touch src/: ws76's
# admission counters and the per-drive TIME_WAIT settling); its toolchain unchanged (wolf
# 0.2.36's archive, the digest below).
LOBO_REV=39788b8658d61e855705cfc7a9a40e1953dae6f6
# px25: lobo's release v0.1.3 (d6bd15b; the trunk commit above was it with
# the channel flipped to +dev), the same toolchain: `tools/mklobo OUT release`.
# px65 (R-px65-3): the release the trunk commit now descends from, v0.1.5
# (91b7613, 2026-10-21), which pins wolf 0.2.33 (pin 85dab5d) / wolf-std
# cceda63: no lobo release is on 0.2.35 yet, so the two builds take two
# wolf archives, each by its own digest (tools/mklobo).
LOBO_RELEASE_REV=91b76133c5bb7eb3ec438cca9f6ebeee1d086fb7
# wolf 0.2.36's linux x86-64 archive (release 427033151), the trunk's (px97;
# 0.2.35's 4cc4045b… until px97); wolf 0.2.33's (release 417610226), v0.1.5's.
# Each read twice from the release API.
LOBO_WOLF_SHA256=d383c74c8cd123b9d9dfaa268271d4f004294f85c2b230237d0ef07027d9500d
LOBO_RELEASE_WOLF_SHA256=4f955e8dfe6eaafa441903eeba43c009c4ec2b45a8da09fe13431e8b12340af8
